 "anterior": "CL025",
 "titulo": "Every night, Roman soldiers built a fort ⛺ Part 2 #history #shorts",
 "capa": "A NEW FORT EVERY NIGHT",
 "descripcion": "After every march, the legion built a fortified camp: ditch, wall, stakes, and tents in perfect rows.\n\nSources: Polybius, Histories 6.27-42; Vegetius.\n\nCould you dig after a 20-mile march?\n\n#history #ancientrome #romanlegion #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "After the march, you don't rest. You build a fort.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The surveyors ride ahead and mark the ground with flags.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every night, a new camp. A ditch, a wall of earth, and your stakes on top.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Four gates, one on each side, always in the same places.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Inside, the tents always go in the same grid.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The commander's tent sits in the middle. Streets run between the rows.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "So every soldier knows his place, even in the dark.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "If the enemy attacks at night, nobody gets lost.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You share a tent with seven men. Your contubernium.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Eight men, one mule, one leather tent.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You eat together, march together, and fight side by side.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You grind your own grain and bake your own bread.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Your centurion carries a vine stick, and he uses it.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "And you drink posca, water mixed with sour wine.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "At night, the guard changes every three hours.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Fall asleep on watch, and your own tent mates may beat you to death.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then one morning, the scouts see the enemy. Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
